<article class="env-construction" id="00BA">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00BA">Construction <span data-tag="00BA">2.3.5.1</span> <span class="named">(The Path Bicategory of a Partially Ordered Set)</span>.</a> Let $(Q, \leq )$ be a partially ordered set. We define a strict bicategory $\operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q]$ as follows: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The objects of $\operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q]$ are the elements of $Q$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Given elements $x,y \in Q$, we let $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{ \operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q] }(x, y)$ denote the partially ordered set of all finite linearly ordered subsets 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ S = \{  x = x_0 &lt; x_1 &lt; \cdots &lt; x_ n = y \}  \subseteq Q \]
</div>
<p>
 having least element $x$ and greatest element $y$, ordered by <em>reverse</em> inclusion. We regard the partially ordered set $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname{Path}[Q]_{(2)}}(x,y)$ as a category, having a unique morphism $S \Rightarrow T$ when $T$ is contained in $S$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every element $x \in Q$, the identity $1$-morphism $\operatorname{id}_{x} \in \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname{Path}[Q]}( x, x)$ is given by the singleton $\{ x\} $ (regarded as a linearly ordered subset of $Q$, having greatest and least element $x$). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For every triple of objects $x,y,z \in Q$, the composition functor 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \circ : \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q]}(y,z) \times \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q]}(x,y) \rightarrow \underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q]}(x,z) \]
</div>
<p>
 is given on objects by the construction $(S, T) \mapsto S \cup T$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>‘ We will refer to $\operatorname{Path}_{(2)}[Q]$ as the <em>path bicategory of $Q$</em>. </p>
</article>
